From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.mediacontrol: MPRIS Seek and SetPosition (6525)

With a timeline from UpdateTimelineProperties, the MPRIS player gets
CanSeek (MaxSeekTime after MinSeekTime). Its Position moves on at the
playback rate while the program plays. Seek(offset) and SetPosition(this
track, position) become PlaybackPositionChangeRequested, at the
timeline's own time and kept within the seekable range. SetPosition for
another track, or past the end, does nothing. When the program's next
timeline jumps by more than a second, a Seeked signal is sent. The
dispatcher raises both kinds of events through one helper.
---
